From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:00:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wintypes: PropertyValue owns its strings, inspectable values
 and arrays, API contract exports

- boxed strings and string arrays keep their own HSTRING copies (the value used the caller's handle, which
  dangled once the caller deleted it); GetString and the array getters hand out copies the caller frees
  (arrays came back as pointers into the value itself)
- CreateInspectable, CreateInspectableArray and GetInspectableArray work
- GetIids, GetRuntimeClassName and GetTrustLevel answer for the factory and for property values
- RoIsApiContractMajorVersionPresent now agrees with IApiInformationStatics, RoIsApiContractPresent is
  implemented; 34 todo_wine marks in tests/wintypes.c that already pass are removed

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XZFS4SPPzeH5d2c1MuzqCS

